#################################
# --- Tutorial
# chassis car
_TM_551 You're installing a general part in the vehicle, where is glue in the 'body' of it.
_TM_552 Feel free to explore well the commands, mainly invert (Z) and centralize (X), may be useful here.
_TM_553 Pressing, for example G+1 you can save position 1, if you want another part in same position and size, use H+1.
_TM_554 Install an spoiler usually requires installing in 'Boot' (trunk) and not in 'chassis'.
_TM_555 Remember that these tips changes dependent the location of you're installing.

# door car
_TM_556 You're installing a part in a door.
_TM_557 If you want to install the same part in other door, remember to save and load position (G+1/2/3/4 and H+1/2/3/4).
_TM_558 Open doors (C) to see/test better.
_TM_559 You can change the door position at 'Move - Nodes' in main menu.
#_TM_560

# trunk car
_TM_561 You're installing a part in the boot (trunk).
_TM_562 If you're installing for example a spoiler, the centralize command (X) may help, press X+~>~ to become in the center.
_TM_563 Open doors (C) to see/test better.
_TM_564 If you're trying to install a part inside the trunk, you didn't understood. The correct way is in 'body'.
#_TM_565

# bonnet car
_TM_566 You're installing a part in the bonnet (hood).
_TM_567 The commands centralize (X) and invert (Z) can be super useful here.
_TM_568 Open doors (C) to see/test better.
_TM_569 To install double scoops, remember to hold Z while accept the part to create a clone in other side.
#_TM_570

# wheel car bike
_TM_521 Apparently you're installing a new wheel. If you don't hid the original wheel, you can in the end of installation.
_TM_522 At the end of installation you have options to install the same wheel on the other side (left-right if car) or at all.
_TM_523 Never edit Y or Z (be position or size) or rotations, otherwise the wheel will wobble! Keep it centralized.
_TM_524 Use X+~u~ and X+PageDown to centralize the position. CTRL+X to centralize the rotation S+X to reset the size.
_TM_525 S+~>~ to enlarge and S+CTRL+~u~/~d~ to increase/decrease. Then go to 'Adjusts > Wheel' to fix wheel sink on ground.

# bike bmx
_TM_526 You're installing a new part on the fork. Or a new fork.
_TM_527 Pay close attention where it is or is not a fork to not install in the wrong place.
_TM_528 The fork on motorcycle dampens, if you don't want to dampen, install it in mudguard.
_TM_529 A bicycle, not dampens only turns.
#_TM_530

_TM_531 You're installing a new part on the bike mudguard.
_TM_532 Pay close attention where it is or is not a mudguard to not install in the wrong place.
_TM_533 The mudguard don't dampens, only turns, if you want to dampen, install in the fork.
_TM_534 Tip: Part in mudguard can be used for example to install a disk brake caliper.
#_TM_535

_TM_536 Apparently you're installing a new pedal or chainset of a bicycle.
_TM_537 Use the command to center the part (X) if you move unintentionally because usually here you don't need change the position.
_TM_538 Installing pedals, may be necessary to save and load the position. And the Invert Size (Z+S+~>~) can also be useful.
#_TM_539
#_TM_540

_TM_546 Apparently you are installing a new handlebar.
_TM_547 You probably will not need to move to the right and left sides. If you do this unintentionally, center using X+~>~
_TM_548 Press to accept the installation for CJ appear on your bicycle or motorcycle and so see if this in the correct position.
#_TM_549
#_TM_550

# plane heli
_TM_541 You are installing a general part in a plane, heli or boat.
_TM_542 If you want to install the part for example in propeller or any other place, go back to choose the part and press 'H'
_TM_543 Feel free to explore well the commands, mainly invert (Z) and centralize (X), may be useful here.
#_TM_544
#_TM_545

# error
_TM_600 ~y~-~w~ Sorry, there is no specific tips for where you are installing ~y~-
_TM_800 ~y~-~w~ Sorry, there is no specific tips for the dummy you are positioning ~y~-

# suspension
_TM_571 ~s~Use ~y~Y~s~ to lift and ~y~N~s~ to lower.~n~Use ~y~G~s~ to tilt to rear and ~y~J~s~ to front.
_TM_572 ~s~Drive with your car while lifting/lowering to smooth movement. Use ~y~H~s~ to go back to the original.
_TM_573 ~s~Use ~y~B~s~ to reset camber. ~y~V~s~ to change camera angle.
_TM_574 ~s~Use the return key (by default ~y~ENTER~s~ or ~y~F~s~) to accept the current suspension.

# springs
_TM_575 ~s~Use ~y~Y~s~ and ~y~N~s~ to adjust the softness.~n~~y~U~s~ and ~y~M~s~ to adjust the length of the springs.
_TM_576 ~s~Use ~y~H~s~ to go back to the original. ~y~V~s~ to change camera angle.
_TM_577 ~s~Don't stiff springs too much to your car don't bug or jumps in low FPS. Increase the softness if this happens.
_TM_578 ~s~Use return key (by default ~y~ENTER~s~ or ~y~F~s~) to accept the current springs.

# wheel
_TM_585 ~s~Use ~y~Y~s~ and ~y~N~s~ to increase/decrease the size of wheels at same time.
_TM_586 ~s~This tool serves to ajust the size of wheel collision. You will also need to install a new bigger wheel.
_TM_587 ~y~U~s~ and ~y~M~s~ for front ~y~T~s~ and ~y~B~s~ for rear. If wheel get tilt, disable camber in 'More' screen.
_TM_588 ~s~Use ~y~H~s~ to go back to the original. ~y~V~s~ to change camera angle.
_TM_589 ~s~Use return key (by default ~y~ENTER~s~ or ~y~F~s~) to accept the current wheels.

# main
_TM_580 ~s~Tip for tip: Use and abuse of ~y~J~s~ key, will help a lot in almost any screen in this mod.
_TM_581 ~s~Use TAB+U to enable/disable, or TAB+i to pass the song. You can add songs in 'cleo\Tuning Mod\Songs'.
_TM_582 ~s~You can configure several things in .ini files located in folder 'cleo\Tuning Mod'.
_TM_583 ~s~Hold V to show the vehicle. Note that you can use the mouse normally and do zoom by using scroll or O and L.
_TM_584 ~s~The main keys of this mod are Y, N, H, G and B. Also SHIFT and TAB also can be used for fast and slower commands.

# dummy lights
_TM_801 ~s~Position of the headlights or taillights.
_TM_802 ~s~Note that in vehicles with double lights, the position will be repeated on other side.
_TM_803 ~r~Change this position will change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy seat front - geral
_TM_805 ~s~Front seat position.
_TM_806 ~sNote that the passenger position will be repeated on other side.
_TM_807 ~g~Change this position will NOT change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy seat front - bikes
_TM_811 ~s~Seat position of the driver.
_TM_812 ~g~Change this position will NOT change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy seat back - geral
_TM_815 ~s~Seat position of the back passenger.
_TM_816 ~s~The position of this dummy is the center position of the two passengers.
_TM_817 ~r~Change this position will change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy seat back - bikes
_TM_821 ~s~Seat position of the croup.
_TM_822 ~r~Change this position will change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy exhaust
_TM_825 ~s~Exhaust smoke position.
_TM_826 ~s~If you have double exhaust activated, the position of the exhaust will be repeated at other side.
_TM_827 ~s~Remember that you can enable the double exhaust at More screen.
_TM_828 ~g~Change this position will NOT change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy engine
_TM_861 ~s~Engine smoke position when the vehicle is damaged.
_TM_862 ~r~Change this position will change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy petrol cap
_TM_831 ~s~Position of the petrol cap.
_TM_832 ~s~When this location be hit by a gun, the vehicle will explode.
_TM_833 ~r~Change this position will change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy hook up
_TM_835 ~s~Position of the frontal hitch.
_TM_836 ~s~This dummy is used on front of trailer, may be useless on other vehicles.
_TM_837 ~r~Change this position will change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy ped arm - geral
_TM_841 ~s~Position where the peoples put the arms at car windows.
_TM_842 ~s~Apparently originally not used by the game.
_TM_843 ~r~Change this position will change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy bar grip - bikes
_TM_845 ~s~Position where the hands be positioned on handlebar.
_TM_846 ~s~The arms will be stretched as needed.
_TM_847 ~r~Change this position will change all vehicles with the same model.

# dummy miscpos
_TM_851 ~s~Position used internally.
_TM_852 ~s~Can be used by several proposes.
_TM_853 ~r~Change this position will change all vehicles with the same model.

# move wheel
_TM_855 ~s~The wheel position can only be changed with 2D, because the Z is constantly updated by the game.
_TM_856 ~s~So, you can't change the height of the wheel, obviously, because the position of the wheel is always the ground.
_TM_857 ~s~Do note also that this position is just visual, will not change the behaviour of your vehicle.

#################################
# --- Tour
_TM_900 ~s~Press -~y~K~s~-

_TM_910 ~s~It's here where all starts! Hold -~y~J~s~- to see tips and learn some commands. Press ~y~K~s~- to continue.
_TM_911 ~s~You may start adding a new part on your vehicle in 'Add Part' at left.
_TM_912 ~s~Note that there are several 'locations' to install the part. This choice means where the part will be 'glued'.
_TM_913 ~s~Practical example: A spoiler may be installed at 'boot', so when the boot opens up the spoiler will go along.
_TM_914 ~s~If you don't know where to install, go to 'body', where the general body of the vehicle is.

_TM_915 ~s~Here you choose the part to install! There are SEVERAL commands available, hold -~y~J~s~- to see them.
_TM_916 ~s~The parts are stored in different .ini files where you can edit. Use the up and down arrows to change the .ini.
_TM_917 ~s~Originally the Tuning Mod only comes with some game objects on .ini, everything gets cooler when you download new parts.
_TM_918 ~s~Literally any game model can be used, even a whole building! As so use a part of some vehicle in other!
_TM_919 ~s~Explore this screen and choose something.

_TM_920 ~s~See the right side of the screen for the number of commands!
_TM_921 ~s~Hold some keys (as S, X, Z etc) and see the commands changing. You can do several combinations!
_TM_922 ~s~For example, holding S and CTRL you can use arrows up and down to change the total size of the part model.
_TM_923 ~s~Remember to control the camera by mouse, as so using zoom with scroll or O and L.
_TM_924 ~s~Note also that, when pressing the up arrow the part will move to the front of vehicle, no matter the camera position.
_TM_925 ~s~If you prefer to move to the front of the CAMERA and not the vehicle, change the command mode using -~y~B~s~-.
_TM_926 ~s~Note that you can also save and load positions (including rotation, size etc) as shown in the screen bottom.
_TM_927 ~s~For this, press for example G+1 to save at slot '1'. Now at any momment use H+1 to go back.
_TM_928 ~s~The use of tips (key -~y~J~s~-) here is also important and changes according to location where you're installing.
_TM_929 ~s~Finally, train and know the possibilities!
_TM_930 ~s~Please, press -~y~B~s~- again to go back to the 'Commands Mode: 1'

_TM_931 ~s~You installed your first part! You may want to go back to the main menu or in 'Manage' see other things.

_TM_935 ~s~Here is a more 'advanced' screen for choose the location to install the part.
_TM_936 ~s~Here is locations where are not listed on menu. May be useful for example to install parts at helicopter propeller.

_TM_941 ~s~Here is the list of all your vehicle parts. Hold -~y~J~s~- to see commands!
_TM_942 ~s~Note that you can hide the parts, as so renaming the parts you installed and other things.

_TM_945 ~s~Done? You can save the changes in your vehicle using command T+M.
_TM_946 ~s~However there are several things you need to understand, be sure to read the Readme file from the mod!

_TM_951 ~s~There are many possibilities, this is where the "bonus" features are.
_TM_952 ~s~There's really a lot you can do here! Explore them.

